  "locations": "Printed p.6 Table 3 (PDF p.7); printed p.14 Fig. 12b (PDF p.15), printed p.15 Fig. 13 and Table 6 (PDF p.16); data statement p.19.",
  "paired_cases": "Natural convection; STFC standard k–epsilon URANS in Code Saturne 8.0 with two-scale and scalable wall functions, both 11,683 cells, y_wall+ >30, same configuration, benchmark DNS and matching grid. These are two RANS wall-treatment variants. In Fig. 12 their traces are blue open circles (two-scale) and blue crosses (scalable). FNC standard k–epsilon EWT is a third case from another participant, solver and mesh, not a substitute for either.",
  "figure_relations": "Fig. 12b plots signed wall stress tau_w [Pa] versus y [m] on baffle-left; the authors single out scalable as failing the rise at the baffle end. Fig. 13 plots heat flux q_w [W/m²] only on the hot and cold walls. Its legend omits both of these STFC standard-k–epsilon runs. The plotted standard-k–epsilon heat trace is FNC EWT. The text explicitly selected models on their agreement in the shear comparison. Fig. 13 alone cannot establish a thermal ranking of the STFC pair. Table 6 is the authors’ coarse joint qualitative categorisation, not a numerical within-pair heat-error ranking.",
  "archive": {
    "doi": "10.5286/edata/979",
